  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Edisi: the price with a knob",
    "overview": "Edisi is the name of the redesign. The idea fits in one line: every page leads with the answer (on a car page, the yearly price), and the reader's no-claim discount (NCD, the discount a Malaysian driver earns for each claim-free year, from 0% up to 55%) is a knob that reprices it. The site's logo repeats the idea: the dot of the \"i\" in the wordmark is the knob, seated at NCD 55% and lifting one step for each lower NCD step the reader has chosen.\n\nThe page is calm: white paper, black ink, black title bars, and one strong colour, magenta, used sparingly. Three pastel tints each have one job: pink for prices, yellow for totals and policy terms, blue for the car itself, what is covered and explanations. Type is two faces with fixed jobs: Gabarito, heavy and friendly, for the price, headings and title bars; Figtree, at regular weight, for everything else. The site is light mode only.\n\nThe frame borrows from the mid-2000s web (three columns with working side rails, boxed modules whose solid title bars state a finding, breadcrumbs, a site-map footer), with modern behaviour: native controls that work without JavaScript, container queries, and motion that only uses transform and opacity.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Answer first: H1, answer box, byline, then intro, on every content template.",
      "One magenta voice: the main button, the chosen state and the logo knob, never as text on a tint.",
      "Colour by job: pink is price, yellow is total or term, blue is the car, coverage and explanation.",
      "Black title bars that state a finding in words already on the page.",
      "Works without JavaScript: the NCD control reprices through CSS `:has()`.",
      "Glass only on navigation, never behind reading text."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three Magenta Things Rule",
        "body": "In any first screen, magenta appears on at most three things: the logo knob, the NCD control (its knob and chosen bar count as one), and the one main button. A second action is an outline button (`.ea-btn-o`, `.btn-outline`). `bun run check:site` check 7 warns when a first screen has more than three magenta fills.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Job Per Tint Rule",
        "body": "Pink is price. Yellow is a total or a term. Blue is the car, what is covered, or an explanation. A warning is white with a 2px ink border and a red heading, never yellow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Links Rule",
        "body": "Links are ink and underlined (1px, offset 0.18em). Magenta and mid-grey are never text on a tint or on a grey chip.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 14px Floor Rule",
        "body": "No visible text is under 14px. `text-xs` is remapped to 0.875rem in `tailwind.config.mjs`, footnote markers are 0.875rem, and check 6 fails any visible text under 14px at 320, 390 and 1280px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One H1 Size Rule",
        "body": "One H1 per page, always `.ea-h1`. No kicker above it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Is Navigation Rule",
        "body": "Blur is used only on the floating navigation capsule. Nothing with reading text sits on a blurred layer. Under `prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce` or `prefers-contrast: more` the capsule turns solid white with a 1.5px ink ring.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** open every content page with H1 (`.ea-h1`), the answer box, the byline, then the intro.",
      "**Do** keep magenta to three things in the first screen: logo knob, NCD control, one main button.",
      "**Do** give each tint its one job: pink price, yellow total or term, blue car, coverage or explanation.",
      "**Do** write title bars as a finding, using only words already in the module.",
      "**Do** keep one value per price element (`.px` with `data-p*`), so the HTML says one thing.",
      "**Do** keep the 14px floor and 44px targets."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put an all-caps kicker or a label above the H1 or above content.",
      "**Don't** build meta strings out of middle dots (\"Sedan · 1.5L · 2024\").",
      "**Don't** make every block an identical rounded card; use modules with title bars, rows and tables.",
      "**Don't** use text arrows (\"→\") as decoration on links; use `Ikon` (`i-kanan`) or nothing.",
      "**Don't** put magenta or grey text on a tint or a grey chip, or make a warning yellow.",
      "**Don't** blur anything behind reading text.",
      "**Don't** rename the legacy tokens (`hijau-*`, `emas-*`, `krim-*`, `stone-*`, `.btn-hijau`, `font-serif`) without changing every template that uses them."
    ]
  }
}
